只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Let Deepseek Harness access the internet seamlessly. / 让 DeepSeek Harness 无缝访问互联网。","id":"gh:1367015901","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-network","slug":"NaivG/dsh-network","topics":["dsh-plugin","http-requests","out-of-the-box","sitemap","ssrf-protection","web-fetch","web-search"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Let Deepseek Harness access the internet seamlessly. / 让 DeepSeek Harness 无缝访问互联网。"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-network"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Let DeepSeek Harness access the internet seamlessly."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"**English** | 简体中文"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"`dsh-network` gives DeepSeek Harness a full web toolkit: five model-facing tools\n(plus an opt-in dow"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"nloader), a **Network** settings section, a sidebar\nweb-search panel, and tool cards that render lik"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"e first-party ones. It replaces\nthe official `tool-web` `web_search` / `web_fetch` with a long-lived"},{"id":"p5s4","text":" loopback\nNode process. It's also ready to use right out of the box."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Requires `dsh 0.1.0.rc2` or later. See One thing to know."},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Quick Install"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"See Installation."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Why this plugin"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness ships `web_search` and `web_fetch`, and they cover the ground\nuntil a long page ret"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"urns cut off at the inline limit; a link to a `.pdf` or\n`.docx` hands the model binary bytes; a feed"},{"id":"p11s3","text":" URL arrives as a wall of XML\ninstead of a list of posts; a task that needs a raw `POST`, an authori"},{"id":"p11s4","text":"tative\nportal lookup, or a file on disk has no tool at all. If the model needs to perform\nspecific t"},{"id":"p11s5","text":"asks, it can only use external tools such as `curl` or `wget`, or write a\n`tmp_xxx.py` script first("},{"id":"p11s6","text":"and there's no guarantee it will work right the first time)."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"The usual workaround is install a browser-automation plugin(e.g.`browser-use`): open\nthe page, snaps"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"hot the DOM or a screenshot, click, scroll, repeat. That is the\nright instrument for a page that onl"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"y works through interaction, and an **expensive**(really)\none for reading text. Every step pays for "},{"id":"p12s4","text":"a fresh page snapshot plus the tokens\nto read it, and the loop only moves as fast as the page render"},{"id":"p12s5","text":"s, so one article\ncan cost many times the context of its own prose while most of those tokens go to\n"},{"id":"p12s6","text":"navigation, banners and markup the reader never needed."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"`dsh-network` was born to fill this gap. Documents and feeds arrive as\nparsed Markdown, one entry pe"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"r feed item, and a body over the inline cap lands\nin a server-side cache the model can page through,"},{"id":"p13s3","text":" so a long page is read in\nfull rather than losing its tail. Search runs an engine chain (Bing →\nDuc"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"kDuckGo → Baidu by default, keyless) that can be pinned to one engine per\ncall, and every hit carrie"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"s a title, link, snippet and date; when the engines\ndisagree, the answer says so instead of looking "},{"id":"p13s6","text":"empty. `http_request`,\n`web_sitemap` and `web_config` cover the jobs the official pair had no tool\nf"},{"id":"p13s7","text":"or, the settings section and sidebar panel make all of it editable and usable\nby hand, and every req"},{"id":"p13s8","text":"uest — including the opt-in downloader — goes through one\nfenced transport: per-redirect SSRF valida"},{"id":"p13s9","text":"tion, IP pinning, private-range\nblocking and a protocol lock. The only cost is one extra Node proces"},{"id":"p13s10","text":"s, owned by the\nplugin, and the `web` seam stays claimed until you uninstall it."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## What you get"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| Tool | What it does |"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"| `web_search` | Searches through the configured engine chain (default **Bing → DuckDuckGo → Baidu**"},{"id":"p16s2","text":") and returns citeable sources (title, link, snippet, date), a summary, a status flag, and uncertain"},{"id":"p16s3","text":"ty notes. An `engine` argument pins one engine for the call. |\n| `web_fetch` | Fetches one HTTP(S) U"},{"id":"p16s4","text":"RL, returning Markdown by default or the raw body on request, with outgoing links and warnings. PDF,"},{"id":"p16s5","text":" OOXML (`docx`/`pptx`/`xlsx`), ODF (`odt`/`odp`/`ods`) and EPUB responses are converted to Markdown."},{"id":"p16s6","text":" Feeds are recognized by their root element — `<rss>`, `<feed>`, `<rdf:RDF>` — and rendered item by "},{"id":"p16s7","text":"item, so RSS 2.0, RSS 1.0 (RDF) and Atom 1.0 read as entries (details). |\n| `http_request` | Issues "},{"id":"p16s8","text":"a low-level HTTP(S) request with full method, header and body control. |\n| `web_sitemap` | Looks up "},{"id":"p16s9","text":"a curated table of **178** authoritative portals in 23 categories (arxiv, MDN, package registries, Q"},{"id":"p16s10","text":"&A;, government, news, video…) by domain, category, priority or free text, optionally returning a pa"},{"id":"p16s11","text":"ste-able digest. |\n| `web_config` | Reads the live dsh-network configuration, or applies a partial p"},{"id":"p16s12","text":"atch once you enable the safety toggle (see Settings). Full behaviour: configuration.md. |\n| `web_do"},{"id":"p16s13","text":"wnload` | **Off by default.** Saves a binary file (image, archive, media, font) to disk and returns "},{"id":"p16s14","text":"its path, on the same transport as every other tool rather than a socket of its own. See Safety for "},{"id":"p16s15","text":"the same transport as every other tool rather than a socket of its own. See Safety for the fences. |"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"`web_fetch` and `http_request` bodies over the inline cap (about 20 KB) return\na preview plus a `cac"},{"id":"p17s2","text":"heId`; the model pages the rest with one more call, and an\noversized feed preview always stops on a "},{"id":"p17s3","text":"whole entry boundary, so it can jump\nstraight to entry 40 without re-fetching the URL. See\nCLI and c"},{"id":"p17s4","text":"boundary, so it can jump\nstraight to entry 40 without re-fetching the URL. See\nCLI and cache paging."},{"id":"p18s1","text":"### Tool cards"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Every tool renders as a first-party-style dsh card — a borderless disclosure\nrow over the result bod"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"ery tool renders as a first-party-style dsh card — a borderless disclosure\nrow over the result body:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"`web_search` tool"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"`web_sitemap` tool"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"`http_request` tool"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"`web_config` tool"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"`web_config` uses the same card. A read collapses to\n`Network config · Read config · N engines`; a w"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"rite expands and lists each\nchanged field **with the value that was stored**, so a field the host cl"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"amped\n(ask for `searchMaxResults: 50`, get `20`) reads as a clamp rather than as the\nrequest, and a "},{"id":"p24s4","text":"write the safety toggle refused shows as an amber *refused*\nblock instead of a silent no-op. The liv"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"e config sits underneath in labelled\ngroups (engine chain with key chips, timeouts, protections, all"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"owlist, caps,\ntool switches, GitHub) above the raw JSON."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"### Support search engines"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"| Engine id | Credential |"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"| `deepseek-official`(HOST ONLY) | DSH native account/credentials (optional; usage may be billed) |\n"},{"id":"p27s2","text":"| `bing` | none |\n| `duckduckgo` | none |\n| `baidu` | none |\n| `so360` | none (IP rate limit) |\n| `g"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"ithub` | token optional |\n| `searxng` | none (your own instance) |\n| `brave` | **keyed, billed** |\n|"},{"id":"p27s4","text":" `mojeek` | none (Altcha-gated) / **keyed, billed** |\n| `tavily` | keyless (rate-limited) / **keyed,"},{"id":"p27s5","text":" none (Altcha-gated) / **keyed, billed** |\n| `tavily` | keyless (rate-limited) / **keyed, billed** |"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"Bing → DuckDuckGo → Baidu is the default chain; the other are opt-in.\nSee Search engines for more de"},{"id":"p28s2","text":" DuckDuckGo → Baidu is the default chain; the other are opt-in.\nSee Search engines for more details."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
